The exact sequence (8) is therefore the projective limit of the homotopy exact sequences (12), which gives in particular
\[
\begin{aligned}
(13)\qquad \pi_{\bar K/K}&\simeq\varprojlim_i\underbrace{\pi_1(\bar U_i,\bar\eta)}_{\pi_i}\\
&\simeq\varprojlim_i\pi_1(U_i(\mathbb C),\bar\eta)^{\wedge}
\end{aligned}
\]
\margin{This interpretation is obviously not specific to the base field $\mathbb Q$ --- it holds \unsure{for|for} every field extension $K/K_0$}

Using the fibrations of the $U_i$ (in the case where one restricts oneself to taking Artin's elementary varieties), one finds that every $\pi_i$ is a group \deleted{\unsure{by}} successive extension of \inserted{$n$} \uline{free} profinite groups (here $n=\dim U_i=\operatorname{deg.tr.}K/\mathbb Q$). This gives again
